  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cleaning water for poor children in Cambodia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Phnom Srouch district, more than 85% of the people ae agriculture as mango that is a potential crop after the rice crop, which is creating opportunities for local people to create jobs through the processing of mangoes and fresh fruits in many places. Yeay Maopichnil commune has 9 villages, Phum Brammouy village is in this commune with 2387 people (540 families). People live here is depending on rainy and underground water for consumption as food, cleaning and agriculture.</narrative>
  </description>
